{"base_rate":0.20866141732283464,"brier":0.14824448818897637,"bss":0.1022114521730968,"bss_hi":0.2255516331455584,"bss_lo":0.0002579411239776352,"chart":{"base":[332.6,72.4],"fp":[271.0,220.1],"lead":"62,236.9 272,211.2 482,170.1 692,121.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.10 — higher than 17% of cities","fp":"low end +7pp, high end +34pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 33% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 3%; promised 70% → rained 54%"},"rel":"62,453.6 82.3,419.4 185.3,326.6 503.1,234.5"},"country":"US","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09780839895013124,"ess":409.9818105858538,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for San Antonio</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The San Antonio rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (91%), believe about\n<b>53%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>3%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nSAN ANTONIO 1.3 ESE, 3.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.10, ranked 177 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(137&ndash;187) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>278</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>86</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>17%</b></td><td class='num'>90</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'><b>54%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>91%</td><td class='num'><b>53%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>San Antonio</b> <span class=\"muted\">United States</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.10</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>137&ndash;187\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    San Antonio &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for San Antonio\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"