21860465116276,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"306.0472440944882\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"306.0472440944882\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,371.52517985611513 63.021860465116276,365.06976744186045 75.50333333333333,321.3333333333333 102.84,275.2266666666667 150.21699999999998,254.60000000000002 229.36394736842107,185.6315789473684 381.33532467532467,188.1818181818182\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 278 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"371.52517985611513\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 86 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"63.021860465116276\" cy=\"365.06976744186045\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 5%&amp;#10;It rained 17% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 90 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"75.50333333333333\" cy=\"321.3333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 13%&amp;#10;It rained 29% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"102.84\" cy=\"275.2266666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 26%&amp;#10;It rained 35% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"150.21699999999998\" cy=\"254.60000000000002\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 48%&amp;#10;It rained 54% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"229.36394736842107\" cy=\"185.6315789473684\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 91%&amp;#10;It rained 53% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"381.33532467532467\" cy=\"188.1818181818182\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(21%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In San Antonio the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.14) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.05).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'>-0.049</td><td class='num'>13.3%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'>0.098</td><td class='num'>13.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'>0.143</td><td class='num'>9.9%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'>0.145</td><td class='num'>0.8%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":29.42412,"lon":-98.49363,"n":762,"n_cities":213,"name":"San Antonio","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":278,"obs":0.02877697841726619,"sig":true},{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.01418604651162791,"n":86,"obs":0.046511627906976744,"sig":false},{"hi":0.09,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.049444444444444444,"n":90,"obs":0.16666666666666666,"sig":true},{"hi":0.19,"lo":0.09,"mean":0.12666666666666668,"n":75,"obs":0.29333333333333333,"sig":true},{"hi":0.35800000000000065,"lo":0.19,"mean":0.2605,"n":80,"obs":0.35,"sig":false},{"hi":0.7289999999999998,"lo":0.35800000000000065,"mean":0.48407894736842105,"n":76,"obs":0.5394736842105263,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.7289999999999998,"mean":0.9133766233766234,"n":77,"obs":0.5324675324675324,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":3.0,"provisional":false,"rank":177,"rank_hi":187.0,"rank_lo":136.975,"reliability":0.02058556981609433,"resolution":0.03929398976610114,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"san-antonio","station":"SAN ANTONIO 1.3 ESE","timezone":"America/Chicago"}